    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "M.124 ALL ABOARD FOR SOUTH AMERICAL MIAMI, FLA.\nPHOTO BY R. B. HOIT\nGIANT 32 PASSENGER PAN AMERICAN FLYING CLIPPER SHIP\n5A-H744",
      "In the comfort of cabins wider than a Pullman\ncar and 70 feet long.\n•Flying Clipper Ships ravelers ride in the great\nof the Pan American\nAirways System—world's largest-which connect\nthe United States, through Miami, with 32 countries\nand colonies of the West Indies, Central and South\nAmerica.\nPOST CARD\n\"C. T. ART COLORTONE\", MADE ONLY BY CURT TEICH A CO., INC., CHICAGO, U.S. A.\nPLACE\nONE CENT\nSTAMP\nHERE"
    ],
